NNAAMMEE
     mmaacc__ppoorrttaaccll — network port access control policy

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile the port access control policy into your kernel, place the
     following lines in your kernel configuration file:

           ooppttiioonnss MMAACC
           ooppttiioonnss MMAACC__PPOORRTTAACCLL

     Alternately, to load the port access control policy module at boot time,
     place the following line in your kernel configuration file:

           ooppttiioonnss MMAACC

     and in loader.conf(5):

           mac_portacl_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The mmaacc__ppoorrttaaccll policy allows administrators to administratively limit
     binding to local UDP and TCP ports via the sysctl(8) interface.

     In order to enable the mmaacc__ppoorrttaaccll policy, MAC policy must be enforced on
     sockets (see mac(4)), and the port(s) protected by mmaacc__ppoorrttaaccll must not
     be included in the range specified by the
     _n_e_t_._i_n_e_t_._i_p_._p_o_r_t_r_a_n_g_e_._r_e_s_e_r_v_e_d_l_o_w and _n_e_t_._i_n_e_t_._i_p_._p_o_r_t_r_a_n_g_e_._r_e_s_e_r_v_e_d_h_i_g_h
     sysctl(8) MIBs.

     The mmaacc__ppoorrttaaccll policy only affects ports explicitly bound by a user
     process (either for a listen/outgoing TCP socket, or a send/receive UDP
     socket).  This policy will not limit ports bound implicitly for outgoing
     connections where the process has not explicitly selected a port: these
     are automatically selected by the IP stack.

     When mmaacc__ppoorrttaaccll is enabled, it will control binding access to ports up
     to the port number set in the _s_e_c_u_r_i_t_y_._m_a_c_._p_o_r_t_a_c_l_._p_o_r_t___h_i_g_h sysctl(8)
     variable.  By default, all attempts to bind to mmaacc__ppoorrttaaccll controlled
     ports will fail if not explicitly allowed by the port access control
     list, though binding by the superuser will be allowed, if the sysctl(8)
     variable _s_e_c_u_r_i_t_y_._m_a_c_._p_o_r_t_a_c_l_._s_u_s_e_r___e_x_e_m_p_t is set to a non-zero value.

